# Lightstall Inquisitor in a game of three: "each opponent exiles a card from their hand" asks Bot2 and then Bot3, in turn
# order from the active player (CR 101.4), and never Bot1, who controls it. Bot3's first card is an Island, so if Bot3 were
# asked first its answer would be the default Island and its Mountain would stay in hand. Each may play only the card it
# exiled itself ("may play that card"): on its turn Bot3 can't play Bot2's Swamp, and plays its own Mountain, tapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Lightstall Inquisitor
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Island x16

[Bot3 Deck]
Island
Mountain
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightstall Inquisitor.Cast
Bot2.Choose(Swamp)
Bot3.Choose(Mountain)
? Exile.Count = 2
[T3 Bot3.Main1]
! Bot3.Exile.Swamp.Play
Bot3.Exile.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot3.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Exile = Swamp
Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
Bot3.Battlefield = Mountain
Bot3.Battlefield.Mountain.Tapped = true
Bot3.Hand.Mountain = (absent)
